module engine where

-- =========================================================================
-- partialEvaluate — the residualizing evaluator (partial evaluation) as a
-- pure `.fenel` walker over the locked 7-case `Expr`. partial-evaluator-
-- substrate Phase 1 (brief:
-- `workstreams/partial-evaluator-substrate/briefs/phase-1-faithful-port.md`;
-- design: `design/partial-evaluation.md`; Step-0 lock:
-- `workstreams/partial-evaluator-substrate/notes/phase-0-step0.md`).
--
-- THE THESIS (Step-0, GO): `partialEval : Expr -> KnownInputs -> ResidualExpr`
-- is source-to-source REDUCTION — given a program and a static prefix of its
-- inputs, compute as much as possible and return a residual `Expr` that,
-- re-evaluated under any extension of the known inputs, yields the same value.
-- It is the faithful port of the 1181-line TS `partial-evaluator.ts` (the
-- parity ORACLE) over `Expr` — the SAME IR as reify / symbolize / solve.
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- PEResult — the ENTITY-FREE internal record `{ done: Bool, value: a }` (the
-- P13/P15/P16 cheap-gate precedent — no new ADT, law count +0, entity oracle
-- untouched). `done = true` ⇒ a CONCRETE runtime value; `done = false` ⇒ a
-- RESIDUAL `Expr`. The `$tag`-tagged Concrete/Residual discrimination is minted
-- at the TS boundary only (`dispatchedPartialEvalDetailed`).
--
-- WHAT COLLAPSES OVER `Expr` (the Fenel-first win, Step-0 D-B): the TS PE's
-- per-JSON-Logic-shape walkers (walkVar / walkIf / walkAndOr / walkConstruct /
-- walkTaggedRecord / walkUserRecord / walkCall / walkKeyAsFnId / walkEagerOp /
-- walkHigherOrderOp) all funnel into the 7 `Expr` cases. `if`/`and`/`or` are
-- `ECall "if"|"and"|"or"`; a construct or pre-tagged value is `EConstruct`; a
-- user record is `ERecord`; every call form (call / |> / apply / key-as-fnId /
-- built-in op) is ONE `ECall`. **`let`/`do` are NOT arms** — they arrive
-- desugared (applied-`ELambda` / sequence), so `walkLet`/`walkDo` subsume into
-- the β-reduce arm (the array-form `{let: [b, body]}` the live PE tolerated is
-- non-canonical + unliftable — dropped with the TS).
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- THE TWO NATIVE LEAVES (ledgered additions to the evaluator-strategies host-
-- re-entry class — `design/ts-exceptions-ledger.md`; engine stays
-- `nativeImplsCtx === {}`):
--   * `peEval jl` — the CONST-FOLD host-`evaluate` re-entry. The Fenel side
--     decides fold-readiness (all leaves concrete-or-`ELambda`), egresses the
--     rebuilt call/construct tree via `exprToJsonLogic`, and hands ONE JL value
--     to the native, which does `evaluate(jl, {}, ctx)` in a try/catch ⇒
--     `Result`. This folds HIGHER-ORDER calls for free (the egressed `{fn:…}`
--     becomes a host closure) with ONE fold native (Step-0 D-4).
--   * `peFnSpec fnId` — the on-demand fn-spec introspection for β-reduce
--     (Step-0 D-3): `Nothing | Just {params, body: Nothing | Just Expr}`, the
--     registry read + the body lift (lift-Err ⇒ body Nothing ⇒ D-inline) done
--     INSIDE the native against the THREADED ctx (so the oracle's extra test
--     fns resolve identically on both sides).
--
-- THE FOLD GATE (Step-0 D-1 — the POSITIVE/pure-SET option, NOT the brief's
-- negative lean). The brief's negative gate (`not (isEffectFnId …)`) assumed an
-- unknown fnId ATTEMPTS the fold and falls to residual on a host THROW. That
-- premise is FALSE: the host `evaluate` does NOT throw on an unresolved fnId (it
-- returns a bogus value), so a negative gate would fold an unknown call to a
-- SPURIOUS concrete value (unsound). So the gate is the POSITIVE
-- `elem fnId foldableFnIds` — the faithful replication of the TS
-- `isPureFunctionRef` (spec-exists ∧ `requires` empty) ∨ (built-in op). The
-- wrapper supplies `foldableFnIds` = every registered fn (by id AND codeName)
-- with an EMPTY `requires`, which naturally includes the built-in op std fns
-- (add / mul / eq / …) and EXCLUDES both effectful fns (non-empty `requires` —
-- stays residual) AND unknown fnIds (not registered — stays residual). This
-- matches the TS oracle exactly on both edge classes. (The Phase-2 `Symbolic`
-- mint still rides symbolize's `isEffectFnId` at the β-reduce arm — Steps 3-5.)
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- CONSERVATIVE MODE (Rom 2026-10-16; plan:
-- `workstreams/partial-evaluator-substrate/notes/2026-10-16-callback-fold-admission-plan.md`
-- § "Conservative repair", with the Astra round-3 amendments). The output is the
-- input program with only safe constant folds filled in; tcb-ledger rows
-- `pe.hof.unknown-callback` (repaired narrowly), `pe.fold.safe-list`,
-- `pe.residual.known-context`, `pe.normalize.harness-semantics`.
--   * FOLD only a call whose head is in the caller-supplied foldable set AND the
--     closed `peSafeFold` list (13 first-order std natives), on concrete
--     quotable arguments; keep only a quotable non-null result. The TS wrapper
--     supplies an EMPTY foldable set under any caller frame other than the
--     exact harness and whenever extraFns are threaded. peEval runs in its own
--     where-proof frame (a failing fold is Err, never an outer trip).
--   * SUBSTITUTE only scalar knowns at single-segment reads; wrap the residual
--     in `$ (\k -> …) v` for each scalar known whose root still occurs
--     (peWrapKnowns). Arrays and objects are never substituted (sharing, code).
--   * PRUNE `if` on a concrete condition only (literal, scalar known or safe
--     fold; peTruthy = json-logic `truthy`); a chain with no live branch and no
--     else keeps its residual no-value `if`. `and` / `or` are NEVER reduced.
--   * KEEP as written (args walked): `let` frames, `$dyn` heads, matches,
--     constructors, records; lambdas verbatim; dotted reads never projected.
--   * NOT CALLED until the later arc (kept as input): peDynCall, peBetaReduce,
--     peBindParams, peAllFoldReady / peFoldReady / peIsELambda, peAndOr /
--     peAndOrFinish, peConstruct, peRecord, peMatchConcrete, peMatchPattern,
--     peMatchCtor, peMatchCtorFields, peExtendBinds; peFnSpec has no caller.
--     The divergence ledger below describes the former full mode: in
--     conservative mode none of D-let, D-λ, D-inline, D-guard's reductions run.
--   * partialEvaluateData keeps constructor / record / list folding through
--     its own bounded walker (peDataWalk).
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- THE DIVERGENCE-CLASS LEDGER — FINAL (Phase 1 complete). The ONLY allowed
-- tag/shape divergences vs the TS oracle; every mismatch lands in one, each
-- asserted-as-expected in `partial-evaluate-port.test.ts`:
--   * D-let    — dead applied-`ELambda` frames DROPPED where TS keeps dead
--                `let`/`do` frames + binding slots (the β-reduce of the
--                desugared chain consumes them). Tier-1 skipped, tier-2 equal.
--   * D-λ      — lambda-valued results: TS mints `Concrete(closure)` (walkFn
--                projects concrete bindings into a closure), Fenel keeps the
--                structural `Residual(ELambda)`. Equal under APPLICATION.
--   * D-inline — β-inlining of fns whose bodies don't LIFT (the adapter's
--                `Err Unsupported` class ⇒ `peFnSpec` body `Nothing`): TS
--                specialises the raw JL body, Fenel leaves the residual call.
--                Tier-2 equal (the residual call re-enters the engine).
--   * D-nolift — the whole-INPUT ingress-lift-fail valve (⊇ the array-form
--                `let` D-arrform): `|>` / `apply` / eager ops / array-`let` /
--                plain-record patterns don't lift, so the wrapper returns the
--                ORIGINAL as residual (identity is always sound). TS may reduce
--                these ⇒ tag can diverge; re-eval equal by identity. ALSO the
--                silent class: `{var: [name, fallback]}` lifts LOSSILY (the
--                adapter DROPS the fallback — flagged platform-wide finding;
--                fallback forms are excluded from PE corpus coverage).
--   * D-guard  — a GUARDED arm under a CONCRETE scrutinee: the TS oracle's
--                matchPatternPE walks `{$guard: …}` as an object key ⇒ never
--                matches ⇒ TS silently SKIPS guarded arms and can select the
--                WRONG later arm (a TS-BUG finding, evidence in the port
--                test). Fenel bails to the SOUND residual rebuild; asserted
--                against GROUND TRUTH (the original's evaluation), not TS.
--
-- STAGED PORT — COMPLETE: Steps 0-2 (pass-through arms + fold seam + control
-- flow) landed 2026-07-03 (`24921ae2`); Steps 3-5 (β-reduce via `peFnSpec` +
-- the applied-`ELambda` let/do recovery + `$dyn:` dynamic-callee resolution +
-- `EMatch` arm-select + the residual-match rebuild) complete the walker.
-- `ELambda` stays a structural pass-through BY DESIGN (closures are values
-- until applied — the D-λ class), matching the TS "don't enter lambda bodies"
-- rule modulo the closure-vs-structural representation.
--
-- NO ENTITY DECLS (the cheapest gate class — the P5/P12/P13/P14a/P15/P16 rule):
-- the walker is structural over the registered `Expr` (7 cases); it declares NO
-- ADTs (PEResult is a plain record), so the entity oracle + ordered list stay
-- UNTOUCHED and the law count moves +0. Only the engine fn roster grows.
-- =========================================================================

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- The public entry. `knowns` is a `{name, value}` list (the reify-env marshal
-- precedent — the wrapper builds it); `foldableFnIds` is the POSITIVE fold gate's
-- set (every registered pure fn by id + codeName — the wrapper builds it);
-- `budget` bounds recursive inlining; `nullValue` is the JS-null sentinel (Fenel
-- has no null literal — threaded like jsonLogicToExpr's `nullValue`). Returns the
-- PEResult `{ done, value }`.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Partial evaluate"
@description "The residualizing evaluator (partial evaluation) as a pure walker over the locked 7-case Expr. Given an Expr, a static prefix of known inputs (a {name, value} list), the foldable-fnId set (the positive fold gate — every registered pure fn by id + codeName), a recursive-inline budget, and the null sentinel, returns a PEResult `{ done, value }` — done=true ⇒ a concrete quotable value, done=false ⇒ a residual Expr that re-evaluates under any extension of the knowns to the same value. Conservative mode (2026-10-16): folds only the closed safe list of first-order std natives on concrete arguments (via the peEval host re-entry), substitutes scalar knowns at plain reads and wraps the residual in a let frame per scalar known still read, prunes if-branches on concrete conditions; and/or, let frames, matches, constructors, records, lambdas and dynamic calls stay as written. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1, conservative repair."
@tags "engine" "partial-evaluation" "reduction" "futamura" "expr" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
partialEvaluate : (expr: Expr) -> (knowns: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
partialEvaluate expr knowns foldableFnIds budget nullValue =
  let r = peWalk expr (peBindingsFromKnowns knowns {}) foldableFnIds budget nullValue
  if r.done then r else peResidual (peWrapKnowns knowns r.value)

-- peJsonLogicToExpr — the PE's ingress (conservative mode, Astra round 4). The
-- shared adapter lowers a missing-else `if` / `?:` to `else null`, but ordinary
-- evaluation of a missing else is a NO-VALUE exit (an enclosing where-proof
-- sees it). So a program holding any `if` / `?:` with an even argument count
-- is refused here; the TS wrapper then returns the ORIGINAL program as the
-- residual (the identity valve, always sound).
@label "PE: JSON-Logic ingress"
@description "The partial evaluator's ingress: Err (⇒ the identity valve, original program kept) when the marshalled JSON-Logic holds any `if` / `?:` without an else (an even argument count — ordinary evaluation exits with no value there, the adapter would write `else null`); otherwise jsonLogicToExpr. partial-evaluator-substrate conservative repair."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate"
@category "engine-internal"
peJsonLogicToExpr : (node: (JsonLogic Any)) -> (ctorDefs: List ({ name: String, fields: List CompileFieldSlot })) -> (nullValue: a) -> Result a (Expr Any)
peJsonLogicToExpr node ctorDefs nullValue =
  if peHasMissingElse node
  then Err (Unsupported { reason = "partial evaluation keeps a missing-else if as written", node = node })
  else jsonLogicToExpr node ctorDefs nullValue

@label "PE: has missing-else if"
@description "True iff a marshalled JSON-Logic tree holds an `if` / `?:` object whose argument array has an even length (no final else), at any depth. partial-evaluator-substrate conservative repair. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate"
@category "engine-internal"
peHasMissingElse : (node: (JsonLogic Any)) -> Bool
peHasMissingElse node =
  case node of
    JlArray { items = items } -> not (all items (\i -> not (peHasMissingElse i)))
    JlObject { fields = fields } -> not (all fields (\f -> not (or (peIfFieldMissingElse f) (peHasMissingElse f.value))))
    JlTagged { fields = fields } -> not (all fields (\f -> not (peHasMissingElse f.value)))
    other -> false

@label "PE: if field without else"
@description "True iff a JSON-Logic object field is an `if` / `?:` operator whose argument array has an even length. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate"
@category "engine-internal"
peIfFieldMissingElse : (f: a) -> Bool
peIfFieldMissingElse f =
  if or (eq f.name "if") (eq f.name "?:")
  then
    case f.value of
      JlArray { items = items } -> eq (mod (length items) 2) 0
      other -> false
  else false

-- peWrapKnownsJl — the identity valve's known wrapping (Astra round 5). When
-- the ingress refuses a program (array-form var, missing-else if, an adapter
-- Err), the ORIGINAL JSON-Logic is the residual; its scalar knowns are bound
-- outermost by `{call: ["$", {fn: [k, prog]}, v]}`, exactly as the outermost
-- data binds them in ordinary evaluation. Non-scalar knowns stay reads
-- (`pe.residual.known-context`).
@label "PE: wrap scalar knowns (JSON-Logic)"
@description "Bind every scalar known (number, string, boolean) outermost around an unchanged JSON-Logic program through the `$` application of a one-param fn, for the partial evaluator's identity valve. Non-scalar knowns are left as reads. partial-evaluator-substrate conservative repair. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate"
@category "engine-internal"
peWrapKnownsJl : (prog: a) -> (knowns: b) -> a
peWrapKnownsJl prog knowns =
  fold (\acc k -> if peScalar k.value then mapSet {} "call" ["$", mapSet {} "fn" [k.name, acc], k.value] else acc) prog knowns

-- peWrapKnowns — CONSERVATIVE MODE (2026-10-16). A scalar known is substituted
-- only at a plain single-segment read the walker reaches; its other uses (dotted
-- reads, reads inside verbatim lambdas and match guards, `$dyn` heads) stay
-- reads. So the residual is wrapped, outermost, in `$ (\k -> residual) (ELit v)`
-- for every scalar known whose name is the ROOT (totSpellingRoot) of a spelling
-- anaSpellingsIn collects (a conservative superset: call heads are listed too,
-- which only adds a harmless binding). Inner binders shadow the wrapper exactly
-- as they shadow the outermost data in ordinary evaluation. Non-scalar knowns
-- (arrays, records, tagged values, callables) are neither substituted nor
-- wrapped: they stay reads, and the residual needs ctx1 ∪ ctx2
-- (tcb-ledger `pe.residual.known-context`).
@label "PE: wrap scalar knowns"
@description "Conservative-mode egress of known inputs: wrap a residual Expr in an outermost single-param applied lambda per scalar known (number, string or boolean) whose name is the root of a spelling in the residual (anaSpellingsIn, roots via totSpellingRoot), so dotted reads, lambda bodies, guards and $dyn heads that still read the known are bound under re-evaluation with the unknown inputs only. Non-scalar knowns are never wrapped. partial-evaluator-substrate conservative repair. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate"
@category "engine-internal"
peWrapKnowns : (knowns: a) -> (residual: Expr) -> Expr
peWrapKnowns knowns residual =
  let roots = map (\s -> totSpellingRoot s) (anaSpellingsIn [] [] residual)
  fold (\acc k -> if and (peScalar k.value) (elem k.name roots) then ECall { fnId = "$", args = [ELambda { params = [k.name], body = acc }, ELit { value = k.value }] } else acc) residual knowns

@label "PE: scalar value"
@description "True iff a value is a host number, string or boolean (Rational / bigint carriers are not numbers here): the only knowns the conservative partial evaluator substitutes or wraps. partial-evaluator-substrate conservative repair. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate"
@category "engine-internal"
peScalar : (v: a) -> Bool
peScalar v = or (isNumber v) (or (isString v) (isBoolean v))

@label "PE: quotable value"
@description "True iff a value is written back as an ELit that ordinary evaluation returns unchanged: null, a number, string or boolean, or an array whose elements are all quotable. Objects of every shape (records, tagged values, single-key operator objects, references) and callables are not quotable. Every concrete PEResult holds a quotable value. partial-evaluator-substrate conservative repair. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate"
@category "engine-internal"
peQuotable : (v: a) -> Bool
peQuotable v =
  if isNull v then true
  else if peScalar v then true
  else if isArray v then all v (\item -> peQuotable item)
  else false

-- peSafeFold — the closed fold list (conservative mode). Each entry is a plain
-- harness native with no ctx-native, no `requires` and only first-order
-- scalar/array params (probed 2026-10-16), listed by canonical id AND code
-- name. Every higher-order function, evaluator re-entry, ctx-native,
-- Fenel-bodied-only function and user function is excluded by construction.
@label "PE: safe fold list"
@description "The closed list of function ids the conservative partial evaluator may fold, by canonical id and code name: std add, sub, mul, div, mod, eq, neq, lt, lte, gt, gte, concat, length. A fold also needs the fnId in the caller-supplied foldable set (empty under any caller frame other than the harness) and all-concrete quotable arguments. partial-evaluator-substrate conservative repair. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate"
@category "engine-internal"
peSafeFold : (fnId: String) -> Bool
peSafeFold fnId =
  elem fnId ["std:add", "add", "std:sub", "sub", "std:mul", "mul", "std:div", "div", "std:mod", "mod", "std:eq", "eq", "std:neq", "neq", "std:lt", "lt", "std:lte", "lte", "std:gt", "gt", "std:gte", "gte", "std:concat", "concat", "std:length", "length"]

@label "Partial evaluate data expression"
@description "Project only literal data, captured constructors, records and source-marked list literals through the existing partial evaluator. Every other expression remains residual; no named function is folded or inlined."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "authoring"
@category "engine-internal"
partialEvaluateData : (node: (JsonLogic Any)) -> (constructorRows: a) -> (nullValue: b) -> c
partialEvaluateData node constructorRows nullValue =
  if peDataInput node
  then
    let defs = map (\row -> CtorDefEntry { name = row.target, wireName = row.wireName, fields = row.fields, ambiguous = false }) constructorRows
    case jsonLogicToExpr node defs nullValue of
      Err error -> peResidual node
      Ok expr ->
        if peDataOnly expr (map (\row -> row.target) constructorRows)
        then peDataWalk expr nullValue else peResidual expr
  else peResidual node

@label "PE: captured data input"
@description "Raw tagged carriers remain residual because constructor re-entry may change their opaque representation. Other source shapes are inspected by the existing core data-fragment gate."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "authoring"
@category "engine-internal"
peDataInput : (node: (JsonLogic Any)) -> Boolean
peDataInput node =
  case node of
    JlTagged -> false
    JlObject { fields = fields } -> peDataInputFields fields
    JlArray { items = items } -> all items (\item -> peDataInput item)
    other -> true

@label "PE: captured data input children"
@description "Preserve the raw source observation of every object child before lowering it to the core data fragment."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "authoring"
@category "engine-internal"
peDataInputFields : (fields: a) -> Boolean
peDataInputFields fields =
  case head fields of
    Nothing -> true
    Just field ->
      if peDataInput field.value then peDataInputFields (tailOr fields) else false

@label "PE: data expression"
@description "The bounded data-expression fragment, using captured constructor targets and the adapter's existing list-literal provenance. Calls, bindings, projections, lambdas and control forms are outside this fragment."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "authoring"
@category "engine-internal"
peDataOnly : (expr: Expr) -> (constructorTargets: List String) -> Boolean
peDataOnly expr constructorTargets =
  case expr of
    ELit { value = value } ->
      if isNull value then false
      else if or (isString value) (or (isNumber value) (isBoolean value)) then true
      else if isArray value then eq (length value) 0 else false
    EConstruct { ctor = ctor, args = args } ->
      and (elem ctor constructorTargets) (peDataOnlyList args constructorTargets)
    ERecord { fields = fields } ->
      if eq (length fields) 1 then false else peDataOnlyFields fields constructorTargets
    ECall { fnId = fnId, args = args } ->
      if and (eq expr.lit true) (and (eq fnId "appendItem") (eq (length args) 2))
      then peDataOnlyList args constructorTargets else false
    other -> false

@label "PE: data expression children"
@description "Every child must remain in the bounded data fragment before the partial evaluator is invoked."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "authoring"
@category "engine-internal"
peDataOnlyList : (exprs: a) -> (constructorTargets: List String) -> Boolean
peDataOnlyList exprs constructorTargets =
  case head exprs of
    Nothing -> true
    Just expr ->
      if peDataOnly expr constructorTargets then peDataOnlyList (tailOr exprs) constructorTargets else false

@label "PE: data record children"
@description "Check record child expressions without admitting callable or reference carrier fields as ordinary data construction."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "authoring"
@category "engine-internal"
peDataOnlyFields : (fields: a) -> (constructorTargets: List String) -> Boolean
peDataOnlyFields fields constructorTargets =
  case head fields of
    Nothing -> true
    Just field ->
      if or (startsWith field.name "__") (startsWith field.name "$") then false
      else if peDataOnly field.value constructorTargets then peDataOnlyFields (tailOr fields) constructorTargets else false

-- peDataWalk — the data-expression projection (partialEvaluateData). The
-- conservative general walker no longer folds constructors or records, so the
-- bounded data fragment (peDataOnly: literals, captured constructors, records,
-- source list literals) keeps its own small walker with the former folding
-- behaviour. It reads no bindings and folds no named function; a constructor
-- runs through peEval in the caller-built execution frame (captured
-- constructor tables only).
@label "PE: data walk"
@description "Project an Expr already admitted by peDataOnly to a concrete value: literals pass, source list literals build the list, records fold field-wise, captured constructors fold through peEval. Any child that stays residual keeps the whole node residual. No bindings, no named-function folds. Internal helper of partialEvaluateData."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "authoring"
@category "engine-internal"
peDataWalk : (expr: Expr) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peDataWalk expr nullValue =
  case expr of
    ELit { value = v } -> peConcrete v
    ECall { fnId = f, args = args } -> peDataList expr args nullValue
    EConstruct { ctor = c, args = args, fields = fs } -> peDataConstruct c args fs true nullValue
    EConstruct { ctor = c, args = args } -> peDataConstruct c args [] false nullValue
    ERecord { fields = fs } -> peDataRecord fs nullValue [] true {}
    other -> peResidual expr

@label "PE: data list literal"
@description "Build a source list literal (the adapter's appendItem marker) from concrete children; otherwise residual. Internal helper of partialEvaluateData."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "authoring"
@category "engine-internal"
peDataList : (expr: Expr) -> (args: a) -> (nullValue: a) -> b
peDataList expr args nullValue =
  let results = map (\a -> peDataWalk a nullValue) args
  let residual = peResidual (mapSet expr "args" (peResultsToExprs results []))
  if and (eq (length results) 2) (peAllConcrete results)
  then
    let item = at results 0
    let items = at results 1
    if isArray items.value then peConcrete (appendItem item.value items.value) else residual
  else residual

@label "PE: data construct"
@description "Fold a captured constructor whose children are all concrete through peEval (egressing the rebuilt EConstruct, named-field metadata preserved); otherwise a residual EConstruct. Internal helper of partialEvaluateData."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "authoring"
@category "engine-internal"
peDataConstruct : (ctor: String) -> (args: a) -> (fields: a) -> (hasFields: Bool) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peDataConstruct ctor args fields hasFields nullValue =
  let argResults = map (\a -> peDataWalk a nullValue) args
  let argExprs = peResultsToExprs argResults []
  let residualExpr =
        if hasFields
        then EConstruct { ctor = ctor, args = argExprs, fields = fields }
        else EConstruct { ctor = ctor, args = argExprs }
  if peAllConcrete argResults
  then
    case peEval (exprToJsonLogic residualExpr) of
      Ok v -> peConcrete v
      Err e -> peResidual residualExpr
  else peResidual residualExpr

@label "PE: data record"
@description "Fold a record field-wise when every field value is concrete (a raw record built with mapSet); otherwise a residual ERecord. Internal helper of partialEvaluateData."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "authoring"
@category "engine-internal"
peDataRecord : (fields: a) -> (nullValue: a) -> (fieldAcc: a) -> (allConcrete: Bool) -> (concreteAcc: a) -> a
peDataRecord fields nullValue fieldAcc allConcrete concreteAcc =
  case head fields of
    Nothing ->
      if allConcrete then peConcrete concreteAcc else peResidual (ERecord { fields = fieldAcc })
    Just f ->
      let r = peDataWalk f.value nullValue
      let fieldAcc2 = appendItem { name = f.name, value = resultToExpr r } fieldAcc
      let concreteAcc2 = if r.done then mapSet concreteAcc f.name r.value else concreteAcc
      peDataRecord (tailOr fields) nullValue fieldAcc2 (and allConcrete r.done) concreteAcc2

-- peBindingsFromKnowns — fold the `{name, value}` knowns list into the opaque
-- bindings map (name ⇒ concrete PEResult), the O(1)-read env the walker threads
-- (the 7h S2 opaque-map perf branch: mapSet/mapGet over the pure assoc list).
-- CONSERVATIVE MODE: only SCALAR knowns are bound (Astra round 3: substituting
-- an array loses the sharing `includes` observes); every other known stays an
-- unbound read.
@label "PE: bindings from knowns"
@description "Fold the {name, value} known-inputs list into the opaque bindings map (name ⇒ concrete PEResult), scalar knowns only (number, string, boolean); other knowns stay unbound reads. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1, conservative repair. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peBindingsFromKnowns : (knowns: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
peBindingsFromKnowns knowns acc =
  case head knowns of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just k ->
      if peScalar k.value
      then peBindingsFromKnowns (tailOr knowns) (mapSet acc k.name (peConcrete k.value))
      else peBindingsFromKnowns (tailOr knowns) acc

-- peConcrete / peResidual — the two PEResult constructors (plain records; NO
-- entity decl — the cheap-gate class).
@label "PE: concrete result"
@description "Build a concrete PEResult `{ done = true, value }` — a fully-reduced value. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peConcrete : (v: a) -> a
peConcrete v = { done = true, value = v }

@label "PE: residual result"
@description "Build a residual PEResult `{ done = false, value }` — an unreduced residual Expr. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peResidual : (e: a) -> a
peResidual e = { done = false, value = e }

-- resultToExpr — project a PEResult back to an `Expr` for residual rebuild /
-- fold egress: concrete ⇒ `ELit value` (the raw value re-wrapped as a literal,
-- exactly what the TS `unwrap` embeds into a residual JSON-Logic tree); residual
-- ⇒ the residual Expr verbatim (an `ELambda` for the fold-ready lambda case).
@label "PE: result to Expr"
@description "Project a PEResult back to an Expr for residual rebuild / fold egress: concrete ⇒ `ELit value`; residual ⇒ the residual Expr verbatim (mirrors the TS `unwrap` embedding a concrete value or residual node). partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
resultToExpr : (r: a) -> a
resultToExpr r = if r.done then ELit { value = r.value } else r.value

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- peWalk — the core PE recursion, structural over the 7 `Expr` cases. The TS
-- `peWalk`'s raw-JSON dispatch (arrays / tagged / single-key / user record)
-- collapses here: `Expr` already separates the shapes.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@label "PE: walk"
@description "The core partial-evaluation recursion, structural over the 7 Expr cases. ELit ⇒ concrete; EVar ⇒ substitute-if-known (dot-path project) / residual; ECall ⇒ if-prune / and-or short-circuit / fold-if-concrete (via peEval) / residual; EConstruct ⇒ fold-if-concrete / residual (fields preserved); ERecord ⇒ field-wise; ELambda / EMatch ⇒ SOUND residual pass-through (β-reduce + arm-select are Steps 3-5). partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peWalk : (expr: Expr) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peWalk expr bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue =
  case expr of
    ELit { value = v } -> if peQuotable v then peConcrete v else peResidual (ELit { value = v })
    EVar { name = n } -> peVar n bindings nullValue
    ECall { fnId = f, args = args } ->
      if and (eq expr.lit true) (eq f "appendItem")
      then peLiteralList expr args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
      else
        let controlIf = and (elem f ["if", "?:"]) (not (eq (lookup expr "structural") (Just false)))
        let ordinaryIf = and (elem f ["if", "?:"]) (eq (lookup expr "structural") (Just false))
        let result = if ordinaryIf then peGeneralCall f args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue else peCall f args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
        if result.done then result
        -- Pruning may return a selected branch, whose own call provenance must
        -- survive. peIf marks only the residual controls it creates.
        else if controlIf then result
        else case result.value of
          ECall { fnId = residualHead } ->
            if eq f residualHead then peResidual (copyCallMetadata expr result.value) else result
          other -> result
    ELambda { params = ps, body = bd } -> peResidual (ELambda { params = ps, body = bd })
    EMatch { scrutinee = sc, arms = arms } -> peMatch sc arms bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
    EConstruct { ctor = c, args = args, fields = fs } -> peResidual (EConstruct { ctor = c, args = peResultsToExprs (peWalkArgs args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue []) [], fields = fs })
    EConstruct { ctor = c, args = args } -> peResidual (EConstruct { ctor = c, args = peResultsToExprs (peWalkArgs args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue []) [] })
    ERecord { fields = fs } -> peResidual (ERecord { fields = map (\f -> { name = f.name, value = resultToExpr (peWalk f.value bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue) }) fs })

@label "PE: literal list"
@description "Consume only the adapter's existing source-list appendItem marker through ordinary list construction. Ordinary appendItem calls retain the function-fold gate."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "authoring"
@category "engine-internal"
peLiteralList : (expr: Expr) -> (args: a) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> b
peLiteralList expr args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue =
  let results = peWalkArgs args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue []
  let residual = peResidual (mapSet expr "args" (peResultsToExprs results []))
  if and (eq (length results) 2) (peAllConcrete results)
  then
    let item = at results 0
    let items = at results 1
    if isArray items.value then peConcrete (appendItem item.value items.value) else residual
  else residual

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- peVar — variable substitution (walkVar), CONSERVATIVE MODE: a dotted read is
-- NEVER projected (dotted reads go through the representation machinery, e.g.
-- `s.length` on a string); it stays a residual EVar and the known wrapper
-- (peWrapKnowns) binds its root. A single-segment read returns its binding: a
-- scalar known (concrete) or a binder's residual self-EVar (shadowing).
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@label "PE: var"
@description "Variable substitution (walkVar), conservative mode: a dotted read stays a residual EVar (no projection); a single-segment read returns its binding (a scalar known, or a binder's residual self-EVar); an unbound read stays a residual EVar. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1, conservative repair. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peVar : (name: String) -> (bindings: a) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peVar name bindings nullValue =
  if gt (length (split name ".")) 1
  then peResidual (EVar { name = name })
  else
    case mapGet bindings name of
      Nothing -> peResidual (EVar { name = name })
      Just r -> r

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- peCall — the ECall dispatcher. `if`/`?:` prune, `and`/`or` short-circuit;
-- everything else (eager ops / higher-order ops / user calls / built-in ops /
-- key-as-fnId — all ONE ECall over Expr) folds-if-concrete-and-pure else stays
-- residual.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@label "PE: call"
@description "The ECall dispatcher, conservative mode: `if`/`?:` ⇒ prune on a concrete condition only; `and`/`or` ⇒ never reduced (they return an operand VALUE, and a dropped operand may be a read a proof sees), operands walked; `$dyn:<name>` heads ⇒ always residual with walked args (the known wrapper binds a scalar known callee); applied single-param ELambda via `$` ⇒ the let frame is KEPT (peApplyLambda); everything else ⇒ a safe-list fold or a residual call. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1, conservative repair. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peCall : (fnId: String) -> (args: a) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peCall fnId args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue =
  if or (eq fnId "if") (eq fnId "?:")
  then peIf args 0 [] bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
  else if or (eq fnId "and") (eq fnId "or")
  then peResidual (ECall { fnId = fnId, args = peResultsToExprs (peWalkArgs args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue []) [] })
  else if startsWith fnId "$dyn:"
  then peResidual (ECall { fnId = fnId, args = peResultsToExprs (peWalkArgs args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue []) [] })
  else if peIsAppliedLambda fnId args
  then peApplyLambda args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
  else peGeneralCall fnId args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue

-- peDynCall — a DYNAMIC callee (`{call: [{var: "f"}, …]}` lifts to
-- `ECall "$dyn:f" […]`). Mirrors the TS walkCall's var-callee resolution:
-- the binding for `f` is looked up — a concrete STRING names a function
-- (re-dispatch as a named call, so inlining/folding apply — TS parity); any
-- other concrete value (a closure) folds via the `$` application vehicle when
-- every arg is fold-ready (`{call: ["$", closureValue, …args]}` — the host
-- curries over-application); an unbound / residual binding keeps the `$dyn:`
-- head residual (the exprToSyntax egress renders it back to the evaluable
-- `{call: ["$", {var: f}, …]}` form).
@label "PE: dynamic call"
@description "Resolve a `$dyn:<name>` dynamic callee through the bindings (the TS walkCall var-callee path): a concrete string re-dispatches as a named call (inline/fold apply); another concrete value (closure) folds via the `$` application vehicle when all args are fold-ready; unbound/residual keeps the residual `$dyn:` call (egress renders `{call: [\"$\", {var: name}, …]}`). partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peDynCall : (fnId: String) -> (name: String) -> (args: a) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peDynCall fnId name args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue =
  case mapGet bindings name of
    Nothing ->
      peResidual (ECall { fnId = fnId, args = peResultsToExprs (peWalkArgs args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue []) [] })
    Just r ->
      if not r.done
      then peResidual (ECall { fnId = fnId, args = peResultsToExprs (peWalkArgs args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue []) [] })
      else
        if isString r.value
        then peGeneralCall r.value args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
        else
          let argResults = peWalkArgs args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue []
          if peAllFoldReady argResults
          then
            let applied = ECall { fnId = "$", args = concat (appendItem (ELit { value = r.value }) []) (peResultsToExprs argResults []) }
            case peEval (exprToJsonLogic applied) of
              Ok v -> peConcrete v
              Err e -> peResidual (ECall { fnId = fnId, args = peResultsToExprs argResults [] })
          else peResidual (ECall { fnId = fnId, args = peResultsToExprs argResults [] })

-- peIsAppliedLambda — recognise the desugared let/do shape: `ECall "$"
-- [ELambda <1 param>, value]` (desugar emits exactly single-binding chains).
-- Multi-param lambdas fall through to the normal `$` path (std:$ is a
-- registered pure fn) — β-reducing a partial lambda application would need
-- unsupplied-param shadowing; the 1-param form is the only shape desugar mints.
@label "PE: is applied lambda"
@description "Recognise the desugared let/do applied-lambda shape `ECall \"$\" [ELambda <exactly 1 param>, value]` — the only shape desugar mints (single-binding chains). partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peIsAppliedLambda : (fnId: String) -> (args: a) -> Bool
peIsAppliedLambda fnId args =
  if and (eq fnId "$") (eq (length args) 2)
  then
    case at args 0 of
      ELambda { params = ps } -> eq (length ps) 1
      other -> false
  else false

-- peApplyLambda — the desugared let/do frame, CONSERVATIVE MODE: the frame is
-- KEPT. The argument is walked, the body is walked with the param bound as a
-- residual self-EVar (it shadows any outer known), and the result is
-- `$ (\p -> body') arg'`: the argument is evaluated exactly once, in order, as
-- ordinary evaluation does (no read or effect is dropped or duplicated). The
-- former β-reduction (D-let) is withdrawn until the later arc.
@label "PE: apply lambda (let/do frame)"
@description "Conservative mode: keep an applied single-param ELambda (a desugared let/do) as a residual frame — walk the argument, walk the body with the param shadowed as a residual self-EVar, rebuild the applied frame (lambda p -> body') applied to arg'. No read or effect is dropped or duplicated. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1, conservative repair. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peApplyLambda : (args: a) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peApplyLambda args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue =
  case at args 0 of
    ELambda { params = ps, body = bd } ->
      case head ps of
        Nothing -> peGeneralCall "$" args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
        Just p ->
          let argR = peWalk (peAt args 1 nullValue) bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
          let bodyR = peWalk bd (mapSet bindings p (peResidual (EVar { name = p }))) foldableFnIds budget nullValue
          peResidual (ECall { fnId = "$", args = [ELambda { params = ps, body = resultToExpr bodyR }, resultToExpr argR] })
    other -> peGeneralCall "$" args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue

-- peGeneralCall — CONSERVATIVE MODE: fold a call only when its head is in BOTH
-- the caller-supplied foldable set (the harness pure set with no caller frame or
-- the exact harness frame; EMPTY in every other frame and under extraFns) AND
-- the closed `peSafeFold` list, and every argument is concrete (a quotable
-- scalar or array). The fold runs through peEval on the call AS WRITTEN; it is
-- kept only for a quotable, non-null value (null is the no-value signal; a
-- throw or a tripped peEval proof frame is Err). Otherwise the residual call
-- with walked args. No β-reduction, no higher-order fold, no callback fold.
@label "PE: general call (fold / residual)"
@description "Conservative mode: fold an ECall only if its fnId is in the foldable set AND the closed safe-fold list (std add, sub, mul, div, mod, eq, neq, lt, lte, gt, gte, concat, length) and every argument is concrete; the peEval result is kept only when quotable and not null (Err or null ⇒ the residual call). Every other call stays a residual call with walked args — no inlining, no higher-order or callback fold. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1, conservative repair. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peGeneralCall : (fnId: String) -> (args: a) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peGeneralCall fnId args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue =
  let argResults = peWalkArgs args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue []
  let residualExpr = ECall { fnId = fnId, args = peResultsToExprs argResults [] }
  if and (elem fnId foldableFnIds) (peSafeFold fnId)
  then
    if peAllConcrete argResults
    then
      case peEval (exprToJsonLogic residualExpr) of
        Ok v -> if and (not (isNull v)) (peQuotable v) then peConcrete v else peResidual residualExpr
        Err e -> peResidual residualExpr
    else peResidual residualExpr
  else peResidual residualExpr

-- peBetaReduce — inline a pure user fn (walkCall/finaliseCallLike's β-reduce):
-- fetch the spec on demand (`peFnSpec` — Nothing / bodyless / lift-Err ⇒ NOT
-- inlinable ⇒ residual call; the lift-Err case is divergence class D-inline),
-- bind known args to params in a FRESH scope (registry fns capture nothing —
-- unsupplied params stay unbound so their body refs stay residual vars), walk
-- the body at `budget - 1` (the recursive-inline bound; 0 ⇒ residual call).
-- args ≥ params ⇒ the body result IS the answer (either kind — extras dropped,
-- MIRRORING the TS over-application behavior); under-application with a
-- residual body ⇒ the specialised body; with a concrete body ⇒ the residual
-- call sentinel (the TS partial-application sentinel — consumers interpret the
-- leftover arity structurally).
@label "PE: beta-reduce (user-fn inline)"
@description "Inline a pure user fn: on-demand spec via peFnSpec (Nothing / bodyless / lift-Err ⇒ residual call — D-inline), FRESH param scope (registry fns capture nothing; unsupplied params stay unbound), body walked at budget-1 (0 ⇒ residual call). args ≥ params ⇒ body result (extras dropped, TS mirror); under-application ⇒ residual body, or the residual-call sentinel when the body reduced concrete. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peBetaReduce : (fnId: String) -> (argResults: a) -> (residualExpr: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peBetaReduce fnId argResults residualExpr foldableFnIds budget nullValue =
  if not (gt budget 0)
  then peResidual residualExpr
  else
    case peFnSpec fnId of
      Nothing -> peResidual residualExpr
      Just spec ->
        case spec.body of
          Nothing -> peResidual residualExpr
          Just bodyExpr ->
            let inner = peBindParams spec.params argResults {}
            let bodyR = peWalk bodyExpr inner foldableFnIds (sub budget 1) nullValue
            if not (lt (length argResults) (length spec.params))
            then bodyR
            else if bodyR.done
                 then peResidual residualExpr
                 else bodyR

-- peBindParams — zip declared param names with PE'd args into a FRESH bindings
-- map. Params beyond the supplied args stay UNBOUND (their body refs stay
-- residual vars — the TS `i < argResults.length` guard); extra args beyond the
-- params are dropped by the zip (the TS over-application mirror).
@label "PE: bind params"
@description "Zip declared param names with PE'd args into a fresh bindings map; unsupplied params stay unbound, extra args drop (TS mirror). partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peBindParams : (params: a) -> (argResults: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
peBindParams params argResults acc =
  case head params of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just p ->
      case head argResults of
        Nothing -> acc
        Just r -> peBindParams (tailOr params) (tailOr argResults) (mapSet acc p r)

-- peWalkArgs — PE a list of Expr children, accumulating PEResults in order
-- (appendItem appends to the END; the symbolizeList idiom).
@label "PE: walk args"
@description "PE a list of Expr children in order, accumulating PEResults (appendItem appends to the end). partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peWalkArgs : (args: a) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
peWalkArgs args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue acc =
  case head args of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just h -> peWalkArgs (tailOr args) bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue (appendItem (peWalk h bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue) acc)

-- peResultsToExprs — map resultToExpr over a PEResult list (residual rebuild).
@label "PE: results to Exprs"
@description "Map resultToExpr over a PEResult list — the residual-rebuild / fold-egress arg list. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peResultsToExprs : (results: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
peResultsToExprs results acc =
  case head results of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just r -> peResultsToExprs (tailOr results) (appendItem (resultToExpr r) acc)

-- peAllFoldReady — every arg is fold-ready: concrete, OR a residual `ELambda`
-- (the higher-order-fold readiness — the egressed `{fn:…}` becomes a host
-- closure, Step-0 D-4).
@label "PE: all fold-ready"
@description "True iff every PEResult in the list is fold-ready: concrete (done), or a residual ELambda (higher-order fold readiness — the egressed lambda becomes a host closure). partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peAllFoldReady : (results: a) -> Bool
peAllFoldReady results =
  case head results of
    Nothing -> true
    Just r -> if peFoldReady r then peAllFoldReady (tailOr results) else false

@label "PE: fold-ready"
@description "A single PEResult is fold-ready iff concrete or a residual ELambda. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peFoldReady : (r: a) -> Bool
peFoldReady r = if r.done then true else peIsELambda r.value

@label "PE: is ELambda"
@description "Recognise a residual ELambda Expr (the fold-ready lambda-value case). partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peIsELambda : (e: a) -> Bool
peIsELambda e =
  case e of
    ELambda { params = ps, body = bd } -> true
    other -> false

@label "PE: all concrete"
@description "True iff every PEResult in the list is concrete (done). Used by the strict EConstruct fold. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peAllConcrete : (results: a) -> Bool
peAllConcrete results =
  case head results of
    Nothing -> true
    Just r -> if r.done then peAllConcrete (tailOr results) else false

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- peIf — dead-branch pruning over the chained `if` arg list (walkIf). Over
-- `Expr` a source `if` is always 3-arg `[cond, then, else]` (desugar emits
-- `ECall "if" [c, t, e]`; a multi-arm chain is NESTED `ECall "if"`), but the
-- port keeps the general chained walk (it degrades to the 3-arg case and stays
-- byte-faithful to the TS residual shape, which reconciles through
-- jsonLogicToExpr's SIf re-nesting). Pairs (cond, then) walk left-to-right;
-- a live known-cond with no accumulated residual collapses to that branch; a
-- dead cond is skipped; an unknown cond appends a residual pair.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@label "PE: if-prune"
@description "Dead-branch pruning over the chained `if` arg list (walkIf): pairs (cond, then) walk left-to-right; a concrete truthy cond with no accumulated residual collapses to the then; a concrete falsy cond is skipped (dead branch); an unknown cond appends a residual (cond, then) pair; the trailing else closes the chain. An empty `out` with no live branch ⇒ concrete nullValue. Rebuilds the smallest residual `ECall \"if\"`. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peIf : (args: a) -> (i: Number) -> (out: a) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peIf args i out bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue =
  let n = length args
  if not (lt i n)
  then
    -- No live branch and no else: ordinary `if` exits with NO value (a proof
    -- sees it), so the residual `if` is kept (`{if: []}` when every pair was
    -- pruned — the same no-value exit), never a concrete null.
    peResidual (mapSet (ECall { fnId = "if", args = out }) "structural" true)
  else if not (lt (add i 1) n)
  then
    -- trailing else at index i (i == n - 1)
    let elseR = peWalk (peAt args i nullValue) bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
    if eq (length out) 0
    then elseR
    else peResidual (mapSet (ECall { fnId = "if", args = appendItem (resultToExpr elseR) out }) "structural" true)
  else
    let condR = peWalk (peAt args i nullValue) bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
    if condR.done
    then
      if peTruthy condR.value nullValue
      then
        let thenR = peWalk (peAt args (add i 1) nullValue) bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
        if eq (length out) 0
        then thenR
        else peResidual (mapSet (ECall { fnId = "if", args = appendItem (resultToExpr thenR) (appendItem (ELit { value = condR.value }) out) }) "structural" true)
      else peIf args (add i 2) out bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
    else
      let thenR = peWalk (peAt args (add i 1) nullValue) bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
      let out2 = appendItem (resultToExpr thenR) (appendItem (resultToExpr condR) out)
      peIf args (add i 2) out2 bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue

-- peAt — index into an Expr list. `std:at` returns the RAW element (or `null`
-- for an out-of-range index — NOT a `Maybe`, unlike `head`), so the valid-index
-- peIf callers use it directly; the `nullValue` param is the documented total
-- fallback contract (peIf's index guards make out-of-range unreachable).
@label "PE: index arg"
@description "Index into an Expr list via std:at (which returns the raw element, not a Maybe). peIf's `lt i n` / `lt (i+1) n` guards keep every access in range. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peAt : (xs: a) -> (i: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peAt xs i nullValue = at xs i

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- peAndOr — short-circuit-aware and/or pruning (walkAndOr). `and`: a concrete
-- falsy short-circuits to that value, a truthy is pruned (identity); `or`: a
-- concrete truthy short-circuits, a falsy is pruned. Surviving residuals are
-- collected; empty ⇒ the operator identity (`and`→true, `or`→false); a single
-- survivor is returned bare (not wrapped in a 1-arg op).
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@label "PE: and/or prune"
@description "Short-circuit-aware and/or pruning (walkAndOr): `and` short-circuits on a concrete falsy (returns it) and prunes a truthy identity; `or` short-circuits on a concrete truthy and prunes a falsy identity; surviving residuals collect — empty ⇒ the operator identity (and→true, or→false), a single survivor returns bare, else a residual `ECall op`. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peAndOr : (op: String) -> (args: a) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> (remaining: a) -> a
peAndOr op args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue remaining =
  case head args of
    Nothing -> peAndOrFinish op remaining
    Just a ->
      let r = peWalk a bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
      if r.done
      then
        let t = peTruthy r.value nullValue
        if and (eq op "and") (not t) then peConcrete r.value
        else if and (eq op "or") t then peConcrete r.value
        else peAndOr op (tailOr args) bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue remaining
      else peAndOr op (tailOr args) bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue (appendItem r.value remaining)

@label "PE: and/or finish"
@description "Finish the and/or prune: empty survivors ⇒ the operator identity (and→true, or→false); a single survivor returns bare; else a residual `ECall op survivors`. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peAndOrFinish : (op: String) -> (remaining: a) -> a
peAndOrFinish op remaining =
  if eq (length remaining) 0 then peConcrete (eq op "and")
  else if eq (length remaining) 1
       then peResidual (at remaining 0)
       else peResidual (ECall { fnId = op, args = remaining })

-- peTruthy — the PE's OWN truthiness (walkIf/walkAndOr's `truthyJs`), ported
-- EXACTLY: null / false / 0 / "" / "0" and the EMPTY ARRAY are falsy —
-- everything else truthy. NOT `std:truthy` (JS `Boolean` coercion — differs on
-- `"0"` and `[]`, both JS-truthy). STRICTNESS (Steps 3-5 fix): the first cut
-- compared with bare `eq`, but `std:eq` is JS-LOOSE (`" " == false` and
-- `[[]] == false` are BOTH true), which flipped whitespace strings + nested
-- arrays to falsy where `truthyJs` (strict `===`) keeps them truthy. The fix
-- discriminates by TYPE first (isBoolean / isNumber / isString / isArray) —
-- loose `eq` is exact WITHIN one type, so each branch is strict-equivalent.
-- BOOL VALUES (2026-10-17): the evaluator's `truthy` now reads the pure Bool
-- value `{$tag:"False"}` as false (`maybe-value.ts` `boolValueOf`). This body
-- needs no such arm because no OBJECT reaches it: a known record value and a
-- `False` constructor both stay residual (measured), and the residual is
-- evaluated by `truthy` itself. Should the PE ever fold records, add the
-- `case v of True -> true | False -> false` arm (the
-- `membershipBooleanVerdict` precedent); `partial-evaluate-port.test.ts`
-- rows `if-bound-false-tag` / `and-false-tag` / `or-false-tag` would catch it.
@label "PE: truthy (walkIf semantics)"
@description "The PE's own truthiness ported exactly from truthyJs (strict): nullValue / false / 0 / \"\" / \"0\" / the empty array are falsy; everything else truthy. Type-discriminated (isBoolean/isNumber/isString/isArray) because std:eq is JS-loose (\" \" == false) — within one type loose eq is exact. Deliberately NOT std:truthy. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peTruthy : (v: a) -> (nullValue: a) -> Bool
peTruthy v nullValue =
  if eq v nullValue then false
  else if isBoolean v then v
  else if isNumber v then not (eq v 0)
  else if isString v then not (or (eq v "") (eq v "0"))
  else if isArray v then gt (length v) 0
  else true

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- peConstruct — the ADT constructor arm (walkConstruct + walkTaggedRecord).
-- PE every arg; if ALL concrete, fold via the `peEval` host re-entry (egressing
-- the rebuilt `EConstruct` through exprToJsonLogic ⇒ `{construct:[ctor, …vals]}`
-- ⇒ the engine's named-field-disambiguating construct). Else a residual
-- `EConstruct`, with the named-field `fields` metadata PRESERVED (dual-arm) so a
-- nested tagged-record residual (`Just {_0 = <residual>}`) round-trips
-- byte-faithfully to the TS walkTaggedRecord shape.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@label "PE: construct"
@description "The ADT constructor arm (walkConstruct + walkTaggedRecord): PE every arg; all concrete ⇒ fold via the peEval host re-entry (egressing the rebuilt EConstruct); else a residual EConstruct with the named-field `fields` metadata preserved (dual-arm) so a nested tagged-record residual round-trips byte-faithfully. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peConstruct : (ctor: String) -> (args: a) -> (fields: a) -> (hasFields: Bool) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peConstruct ctor args fields hasFields bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue =
  let argResults = peWalkArgs args bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue []
  let argExprs = peResultsToExprs argResults []
  let residualExpr =
        if hasFields
        then EConstruct { ctor = ctor, args = argExprs, fields = fields }
        else EConstruct { ctor = ctor, args = argExprs }
  if peAllConcrete argResults
  then
    case peEval (exprToJsonLogic residualExpr) of
      Ok v -> peConcrete v
      Err e -> peResidual residualExpr
  else peResidual residualExpr

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- peRecord — the user-record arm (walkUserRecord). PE every field value; if ALL
-- concrete, surface a concrete record (the raw `{name: value}` map, built via
-- mapSet — the TS `walkUserRecord` returns a raw object); else a residual
-- `ERecord` with PE'd field exprs. Threads BOTH accumulators (the residual
-- `{name, value}` field list AND the concrete record) so ONE pass covers both.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@label "PE: record"
@description "The user-record arm (walkUserRecord): PE every field value; all concrete ⇒ a concrete raw record (built via mapSet); else a residual ERecord with PE'd field exprs. One pass threads both the residual field list and the concrete record. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peRecord : (fields: a) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> (fieldAcc: a) -> (allConcrete: Bool) -> (concreteAcc: a) -> a
peRecord fields bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue fieldAcc allConcrete concreteAcc =
  case head fields of
    Nothing ->
      if allConcrete then peConcrete concreteAcc else peResidual (ERecord { fields = fieldAcc })
    Just f ->
      let r = peWalk f.value bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
      let fieldAcc2 = appendItem { name = f.name, value = resultToExpr r } fieldAcc
      let allConcrete2 = and allConcrete r.done
      let concreteAcc2 = if r.done then mapSet concreteAcc f.name r.value else concreteAcc
      peRecord (tailOr fields) bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue fieldAcc2 allConcrete2 concreteAcc2

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- peMatch — the EMatch arm, CONSERVATIVE MODE: never reduced. The scrutinee
-- is walked and the match is rebuilt (peMatchResidual): every arm body is PE'd
-- under pattern-var SHADOWS (each PatVar name rebinds to a residual self-EVar,
-- so outer knowns don't leak into positions the runtime will rebind), patterns
-- and guards preserved VERBATIM (the known wrapper binds a guard's known reads).
-- The concrete-scrutinee arm selection (peMatchConcrete / peMatchPattern, with
-- its loose-literal and D-guard caveats) is NOT called until the later arc.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@label "PE: match"
@description "The EMatch arm, conservative mode: walk the scrutinee and rebuild the match residually — every arm body PE'd under pattern-var shadows, patterns and guards verbatim. No arm selection. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1, conservative repair. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peMatch : (sc: a) -> (arms: a) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peMatch sc arms bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue =
  let scrutR = peWalk sc bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
  peMatchResidual (resultToExpr scrutR) arms bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue

@label "PE: match (concrete scrutinee)"
@description "Walk arms in order against a concrete scrutinee: guarded arm ⇒ residual bail (the D-guard sound fence); pattern verdict match ⇒ extend bindings with the concrete captures and PE that body only; no ⇒ next arm; unknown ⇒ residual bail; exhausted ⇒ concrete nullValue. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peMatchConcrete : (scrutVal: a) -> (remaining: a) -> (allArms: a) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peMatchConcrete scrutVal remaining allArms bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue =
  case head remaining of
    Nothing -> peConcrete nullValue
    Just arm ->
      case lookup arm "guard" of
        Just g -> peMatchResidual (ELit { value = scrutVal }) allArms bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
        Nothing ->
          let verdict = peMatchPattern scrutVal arm.pattern nullValue
          if eq verdict.kind "match"
          then peWalk arm.body (peExtendBinds bindings verdict.binds) foldableFnIds budget nullValue
          else if eq verdict.kind "no"
          then peMatchConcrete scrutVal (tailOr remaining) allArms bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue
          else peMatchResidual (ELit { value = scrutVal }) allArms bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue

-- peMatchPattern — the 3-way pure pattern matcher over the Pattern ADT vs a
-- CONCRETE runtime value. Verdict record `{kind: "match"|"no"|"unknown",
-- binds: [{name, value}]}`. PatWildcard / PatLit "_" ⇒ match; PatVar ⇒ bind the
-- whole scrutinee; PatLit ⇒ value equality (std:eq — loose across types, exact
-- within one; cross-type literal patterns are a documented caveat vs the TS
-- strict `===`); PatConstruct ⇒ Bool-opaque True/False against JS booleans,
-- else `$tag` compare (a mapGet READ of the `$`-key — reading is legal, only
-- authoring is barred) + per-field sub-match: fields-present ⇒ the declared
-- resolved slots' current wireName; fields-ABSENT ⇒ the positional `_i` convention, where a MISSING key is
-- verdict `unknown` (the pattern may carry lost source-side names — the
-- shouldUseNamedFields gate drops them at lift; assuming `_i` there would
-- wrongly skip arms the runtime matches, so the walker bails to residual).
@label "PE: match pattern"
@description "3-way pure pattern matcher (Pattern ADT vs concrete value): {kind: match|no|unknown, binds}. Wildcard/PatLit \"_\" ⇒ match; PatVar ⇒ bind; PatLit ⇒ eq (loose-across-types caveat documented); PatConstruct ⇒ Bool-opaque + $tag compare + per-field recurse (fields-present = resolved CompileFieldSlot metadata projected to wireName only at the concrete-object read; fields-absent = positional _i with missing-key ⇒ unknown — the lost-names sound bail). partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peMatchPattern : (scrut: a) -> (pat: a) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peMatchPattern scrut pat nullValue =
  case pat of
    PatWildcard -> { kind = "match", binds = [] }
    PatVar { name = n } -> { kind = "match", binds = [{ name = n, value = scrut }] }
    PatLit { value = v } ->
      if eq v "_"
      then { kind = "match", binds = [] }
      else if eq v scrut then { kind = "match", binds = [] } else { kind = "no", binds = [] }
    PatConstruct { ctor = c, args = as, fields = fs } -> peMatchCtor scrut c as fs true nullValue
    PatConstruct { ctor = c, args = as } -> peMatchCtor scrut c as [] false nullValue

@label "PE: match constructor"
@description "Constructor-pattern match: Bool-opaque True/False against a JS-boolean scrutinee (type-gated first — loose eq would coerce); otherwise mapGet the scrutinee's $tag (a non-record scrutinee reads Nothing ⇒ no), compare to the ctor, then per-field sub-match. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peMatchCtor : (scrut: a) -> (c: String) -> (as: a) -> (fs: a) -> (hasFields: Bool) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peMatchCtor scrut c as fs hasFields nullValue =
  if isBoolean scrut
  then
    if eq c "True"
    then (if eq scrut true then { kind = "match", binds = [] } else { kind = "no", binds = [] })
    else if eq c "False"
    then (if eq scrut false then { kind = "match", binds = [] } else { kind = "no", binds = [] })
    else { kind = "no", binds = [] }
  else
    case mapGet scrut "$tag" of
      Nothing -> { kind = "no", binds = [] }
      Just t ->
        if eq t c
        then peMatchCtorFields scrut as fs hasFields 0 [] nullValue
        else { kind = "no", binds = [] }

@label "PE: match constructor fields"
@description "Per-field sub-pattern walk of a tag-matched constructor: fields-present walks resolved CompileFieldSlot metadata in parallel and projects slot.wireName only for mapGet; an invalid/missing semantic slot is UNKNOWN. Fields-absent uses positional `_i` (a missing key there is UNKNOWN, the lost-names sound bail; a missing resolved wire projection is a genuine no). Sub-verdicts propagate; binds accumulate. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peMatchCtorFields : (scrut: a) -> (as: a) -> (fs: a) -> (hasFields: Bool) -> (i: Number) -> (binds: a) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peMatchCtorFields scrut as fs hasFields i binds nullValue =
  case head as of
    Nothing -> { kind = "match", binds = binds }
    Just sub ->
      let projection =
            if hasFields
            then
              case head fs of
                Nothing -> Nothing
                Just slot ->
                  if fieldKeyValid slot.key
                  then Just { wireName = slot.wireName, rest = tailOr fs }
                  else Nothing
            else Just { wireName = concat "_" (toString i), rest = fs }
      case projection of
        Nothing -> { kind = "unknown", binds = [] }
        Just projected ->
          case mapGet scrut projected.wireName of
            Nothing ->
              if hasFields
              then { kind = "no", binds = [] }
              else { kind = "unknown", binds = [] }
            Just sv ->
              let subV = peMatchPattern sv sub nullValue
              if eq subV.kind "match"
              then peMatchCtorFields scrut (tailOr as) projected.rest hasFields (add i 1) (concat binds subV.binds) nullValue
              else subV

@label "PE: extend bindings"
@description "Fold a capture-binds list `[{name, value}]` into the bindings map as concrete PEResults. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peExtendBinds : (bindings: a) -> (binds: a) -> a
peExtendBinds bindings binds =
  case head binds of
    Nothing -> bindings
    Just b -> peExtendBinds (mapSet bindings b.name (peConcrete b.value)) (tailOr binds)

@label "PE: match (residual rebuild)"
@description "Rebuild a residual EMatch: every arm body PE'd under pattern-var shadows (PatVar names rebound to residual self-EVars so outer knowns don't substitute into runtime-rebound positions), patterns + guards preserved VERBATIM (guards are not PE'd — the TS mirror). partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peMatchResidual : (scrutExpr: a) -> (arms: a) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> a
peMatchResidual scrutExpr arms bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue =
  peResidual (EMatch { scrutinee = scrutExpr, arms = peMatchArmsResidual arms bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue [] })

@label "PE: match arms (residual walk)"
@description "Walk EMatch arms for the residual rebuild: shadow the arm's pattern vars, PE the body, preserve pattern + guard verbatim. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peMatchArmsResidual : (arms: a) -> (bindings: a) -> (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (budget: Number) -> (nullValue: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
peMatchArmsResidual arms bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue acc =
  case head arms of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just arm ->
      let inner = pePatternShadows arm.pattern bindings
      let bodyR = peWalk arm.body inner foldableFnIds budget nullValue
      let armOut =
            case lookup arm "guard" of
              Just g -> { pattern = arm.pattern, guard = g, body = resultToExpr bodyR }
              Nothing -> { pattern = arm.pattern, body = resultToExpr bodyR }
      peMatchArmsResidual (tailOr arms) bindings foldableFnIds budget nullValue (appendItem armOut acc)

@label "PE: pattern shadows"
@description "Collect every name a pattern would bind and rebind each to a residual self-EVar in the bindings map (the addPatternVarBindings port) — shadows outer knowns inside a residual match arm's body. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
pePatternShadows : (pat: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
pePatternShadows pat acc =
  case pat of
    PatVar { name = n } -> mapSet acc n (peResidual (EVar { name = n }))
    PatConstruct { args = as } -> pePatternShadowsList as acc
    other -> acc

@label "PE: pattern shadows (list)"
@description "pePatternShadows over a sub-pattern list. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
pePatternShadowsList : (pats: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
pePatternShadowsList pats acc =
  case head pats of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just p -> pePatternShadowsList (tailOr pats) (pePatternShadows p acc)

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- exprToSyntax / exprToJsonLogic — the EGRESS. `Expr`'s 7 cases embed 1:1 into
-- `Syntax`'s 7 core mirrors; `exprToJsonLogic = syntaxToJsonLogic ∘ exprToSyntax`
-- renders a residual back to JSON-Logic (the fold-egress + the tier-2 re-eval
-- surface). Match-arm patterns pass through as raw `Pattern` ADT values (the TS
-- marshal authors their `$tag`/`$bind` — same discipline as syntaxToJsonLogic).
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@label "PE: is lazy op"
@description "Recognise a lazy control-flow op head (`if` / `?:` / `and` / `or`) — the ops that must egress as the op-KEY form (`{if:[…]}`) rather than the strict call form, to preserve lazy / short-circuit re-evaluation semantics. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "egress" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peIsLazyOp : (fnId: String) -> Bool
peIsLazyOp fnId = or (or (eq fnId "if") (eq fnId "?:")) (or (eq fnId "and") (eq fnId "or"))

@label "Expr to Syntax"
@description "Inject an Expr into Syntax — the trivial 7-case identity mapping (ELit⇒SLit, EVar⇒SVar, ECall⇒SCall, ELambda⇒SLambda, EMatch⇒SMatch, EConstruct⇒SConstruct dual-arm, ERecord⇒SRecord); sub-trees recursed, match-arm patterns + named-field `fields` metadata passed through. The residual-egress front half of exprToJsonLogic. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1."
@tags "engine" "ir" "partial-evaluation" "egress" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
exprToSyntax : (e: Expr) -> Syntax
exprToSyntax e =
  case e of
    ELit { value = v } -> SLit { value = v }
    EVar { name = n } -> SVar { name = n }
    -- `if`/`?:` keep legacy structural egress only without an ordinary-call
    -- marker. Fresh control calls carry their
    -- adapter's true/false provenance through SCall, whose inverse distinguishes
    -- raw lazy controls from ordinary eager calls. Only an absent Boolean
    -- mark keeps the legacy hand-Expr SOp convention. A residual `if` chain
    -- may have any arity; every ordinary call keeps the call-form egress.
    ECall { fnId = f, args = args } ->
      -- A source list literal (the adapter's `lit` appendItem chain) egresses
      -- as a JSON array literal of its items' JSON-Logic, IN SOURCE ORDER: the
      -- former `{call: ["appendItem", last, prefix]}` rendering evaluated the
      -- last item first (reordering effects) and looked `appendItem` up in the
      -- re-evaluating frame. (Conservative repair, Astra round 4 effect-trace
      -- test.) SLit's value passes through syntaxToJsonLogic unchanged.
      case peLitListItems e of
        Just items -> SLit { value = map (\item -> exprToJsonLogic item) items }
        Nothing ->
          if and (elem f ["if", "?:", "and", "or"]) (not (eq (lookup e "structural") Nothing))
          then copyCallMetadata e (SCall { fnId = f, args = exprToSyntaxList args [] })
          else if peIsLazyOp f
          then SOp { op = f, operands = exprToSyntaxList args [] }
          -- A `$dyn:<name>` dynamic-callee head (jsonLogicToExpr's lift of
          -- `{call: [{var: name}, …]}`) is NOT an evaluable fnId — render it back
          -- through the `$` application vehicle: `{call: ["$", {var: name}, …args]}`
          -- (std:$ applies; the host curries over-application), which re-evaluates
          -- to the original dynamic call's semantics.
          else if startsWith f "$dyn:"
          then SCall { fnId = "$", args = concat (appendItem (SVar { name = slice f 5 (length f) }) []) (exprToSyntaxList args []) }
          else copyCallMetadata e (SCall { fnId = f, args = exprToSyntaxList args [] })
    ELambda { params = ps, body = bd } -> SLambda { params = ps, body = exprToSyntax bd }
    EMatch { scrutinee = sc, arms = arms } -> SMatch { scrutinee = exprToSyntax sc, arms = exprToSyntaxArms arms [] }
    -- Named-field EConstruct egress: PositionalField identity in ordinal order
    -- keeps the positional emission (aligned by definition), but GENUINELY-named
    -- fields must egress as the single-record-arg form
    -- `{construct: [ctor, {name: val…}]}` — the positional emission would
    -- MISALIGN when the named subset skips a declared middle field (the engine
    -- assigns positionally in declaration order). The record form is probe-
    -- verified to construct identically for both named and `_0` ctors.
    EConstruct { ctor = c, args = args, fields = fs } ->
      if pePositionalFields fs 0
      then SConstruct { ctor = c, args = exprToSyntaxList args [] }
      else SConstruct { ctor = c, args = appendItem (SRecord { fields = peZipFields fs args [] }) [] }
    EConstruct { ctor = c, args = args } -> SConstruct { ctor = c, args = exprToSyntaxList args [] }
    ERecord { fields = fs } -> SRecord { fields = exprToSyntaxFields fs [] }

@label "PE: list literal items"
@description "The items, in source order, of a source list literal: the adapter's `lit = true` appendItem chain ending in the empty-list literal or in a folded concrete prefix (each element one item). Nothing for any other shape. Internal helper of the egress."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "egress" "partial-evaluator-substrate"
@category "engine-internal"
peLitListItems : (e: Expr) -> Maybe a
peLitListItems e =
  case e of
    -- The tail is the empty source literal or a prefix peLiteralList already
    -- folded to a concrete quotable array: each element becomes its own item.
    ELit { value = v } -> if and (isArray v) (peQuotable v) then Just (map (\x -> ELit { value = x }) v) else Nothing
    ECall { fnId = f, args = args } ->
      if and (eq (lookup e "lit") (Just true)) (and (eq f "appendItem") (eq (length args) 2))
      then
        case peLitListItems (at args 1) of
          Just items -> Just (appendItem (at args 0) items)
          Nothing -> Nothing
      else Nothing
    other -> Nothing

@label "Expr to Syntax list"
@description "Inject a list of Expr children into Syntax (ECall.args / EConstruct.args), preserving order. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "egress" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
exprToSyntaxList : (exprs: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
exprToSyntaxList exprs acc =
  case head exprs of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just h -> exprToSyntaxList (tailOr exprs) (appendItem (exprToSyntax h) acc)

@label "Expr to Syntax arms"
@description "Inject EMatch arms into SMatch arms — pattern passed through untouched (raw Pattern ADT value for the TS marshal), body injected, guard preserved when present. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "egress" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
exprToSyntaxArms : (arms: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
exprToSyntaxArms arms acc =
  case head arms of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just arm ->
      let armOut =
            case lookup arm "guard" of
              Just g -> { pattern = arm.pattern, guard = exprToSyntax g, body = exprToSyntax arm.body }
              Nothing -> { pattern = arm.pattern, body = exprToSyntax arm.body }
      exprToSyntaxArms (tailOr arms) (appendItem armOut acc)

@label "Expr to Syntax fields"
@description "Inject ERecord fields into SRecord fields — field name preserved, value injected. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "egress" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
exprToSyntaxFields : (fields: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
exprToSyntaxFields fields acc =
  case head fields of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just f -> exprToSyntaxFields (tailOr fields) (appendItem { name = f.name, value = exprToSyntax f.value } acc)

@label "PE: positional fields"
@description "True iff a resolved fields metadata list is the PositionalField-key prefix 0, 1, … (or empty) — the case where positional construct emission stays aligned. Current wire spelling is irrelevant to structural positional identity. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "egress" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
pePositionalFields : (fs: a) -> (i: Number) -> Bool
pePositionalFields fs i =
  case head fs of
    Nothing -> true
    Just f ->
      case f.key of
        PositionalField { index = fieldIndex } ->
          if eq fieldIndex i
          then pePositionalFields (tailOr fs) (add i 1)
          else false
        NamedField -> false

@label "PE: zip construct fields"
@description "Zip an EConstruct's resolved named-field metadata with its args into SRecord `{name, value}` fields, projecting each semantic slot's current wireName only at this source/property egress boundary. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "partial-evaluation" "egress" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
peZipFields : (fs: a) -> (args: a) -> (acc: a) -> a
peZipFields fs args acc =
  case head fs of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just field ->
      case head args of
        Nothing -> acc
        Just a -> peZipFields (tailOr fs) (tailOr args) (appendItem { name = field.wireName, value = exprToSyntax a } acc)

@label "Expr to JSON Logic"
@description "Render a residual Expr back to JSON-Logic — the composition `syntaxToJsonLogic ∘ exprToSyntax`. The fold-egress (peEval hands the rendered call tree to the host evaluate) + the tier-2 re-eval surface. partial-evaluator-substrate Phase 1."
@tags "engine" "ir" "partial-evaluation" "egress" "partial-evaluator-substrate" "phase-1"
exprToJsonLogic : (e: Expr) -> a
exprToJsonLogic e = syntaxToJsonLogic (exprToSyntax e)

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- normalizeForDecide — PE-AS-NORMALIZER (decide-substrate Phase 7). The
-- reduction half of Curry-Howard, made a pipeline stage: run the Fenel-bodied
-- `partialEvaluate` over a predicate `Expr` (NO known inputs — the free reads
-- stay residual calls, Phase-2 D-A) and project the PEResult back to an `Expr`
-- (`resultToExpr` — a folded concrete value re-wraps as `ELit`). The branching
-- faces (satSymbolicPaths / solveSymbolicPaths) run this BEFORE the gate / mint
-- / fork:
--   • const-folds (`(2+3)*read k == 10` ⇒ `5*read k == 10`, so the P12 affine
--     inversion witnesses 2 where the un-folded `mul(add(2,3),r)` is opaque);
--   • prunes concretely-dead if-branches (a folded-false cond kills its arm
--     BEFORE forking — dead writes no longer poison the reads-only gate);
--   • collapses a whole-concrete predicate to `ELit false` (⇒ forkResidualFalse
--     fires ⇒ Just false) or `ELit true` (⇒ no atoms ⇒ Nothing, never Just true).
-- SOUND + strictly wider: the PE is semantics-preserving (the Phase-1 oracle
-- contract — the residual re-evaluates to the same value under any extension of
-- the knowns) and preserves effect sites as residual calls, so gating on the
-- RESIDUAL is sound (a PE-pruned write sat in a concretely-dead branch that never
-- executes). `budget` is the fixed DEFAULT_PE_BUDGET literal 8 (the value the
-- engine-bodies-dispatch.ts PE wrapper threads as `_partialBudget ?? 8`).
-- `nullValue` = the JS-null sentinel (marshal-supplied, like partialEvaluate).
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label "Normalize for decide"
@description "PE-as-normalizer (decide-substrate Phase 7): run `partialEvaluate` over a predicate Expr with NO known inputs (free reads stay residual calls) at the fixed PE budget 8, then project the PEResult back to an Expr (resultToExpr — a folded concrete value re-wraps as ELit). Const-folds pure sub-terms, prunes concretely-dead if-branches, and collapses a whole-concrete predicate to a boolean ELit — the reduction half made a pipeline stage the branching faces run before gate/mint/fork. Semantics-preserving (the Phase-1 oracle contract) and effect-site-preserving, so gating on the residual is sound and strictly wider. decide-substrate Phase 7."
@tags "engine" "partial-evaluation" "normalize" "decide-substrate" "phase-7" "fork-exec"
normalizeForDecide : (foldableFnIds: List String) -> (nullValue: a) -> (expr: Expr) -> Expr
normalizeForDecide foldableFnIds nullValue expr =
  resultToExpr (partialEvaluate expr [] foldableFnIds 8 nullValue)
